# Files to exclude from the VSIX package.
# vsce packages everything NOT listed here, so the package contains only:
#   package.json, package.nls*.json, out/extension/, out/webview/,
#   icons/, README*.md, SUPPORT*.md, SECURITY*.md, CHANGELOG*.md, LICENSE,
#   node_modules/better-sqlite3/** (minus its build-time sources).
#
# The database engine is SQLite itself, via `better-sqlite3`, a NATIVE local-file
# engine that reads and writes the shared `SQLite format 3` container. sql.js is
# gone (out/vendor/sqljs/ and node_modules/sql.js must never ship), and so are
# @libsql/** and libsql/** — replaced wholesale. `@libsql/client-wasm` was also
# evaluated and rejected: it cannot open a file (absolute paths fail with
# SQLITE_CANTOPEN and a relative one silently becomes an in-memory DB that never
# reaches disk).
#
# node_modules is excluded by default, but the engine is re-included via the `!`
# overrides below — the installed extension loads it directly from node_modules.
#
# MULTI-PLATFORM: unlike the native engines that publish one optional package per
# platform, `better-sqlite3` ships EVERY platform's prebuilt binary inside the one
# package (`prebuilds/<platform>-<arch>.node`, eight of them). A single VSIX
# therefore serves all of them, and `vsce package --target` is no longer required
# to produce a working artifact. Resolution happens at require time in
# `lib/binding.js` from `process.platform` / `process.arch`, with musl detected
# separately for Linux.
.vscodeignore
.gitignore
node_modules/**
# The engine is re-included by naming the paths it actually needs, NOT by
# re-including the whole package. This matters: vsce applies these globs with a
# parent-directory inclusion (`!node_modules/better-sqlite3/**`) winning over any
# later attempt to exclude a child, so the "include all, then exclude the
# build-time sources" shape silently shipped ~5.4 MB of C++/C sources. Listing the
# needed paths positively is the only shape that prunes reliably.
#
#   prebuilds/  every platform's prebuilt binary, resolved at require time
#   lib/        the JS wrapper that does the resolving
#   package.json  the package's own `main`/`exports` entry points
#   LICENSE       the MIT text, which must travel with the binary
#
# Everything else in the package — `deps/` (vendored SQLite C sources), `src/`
# (the addon's C++ sources), `binding.gyp`, `README.md` — exists only so `npm
# install` can compile from scratch, which every supported platform avoids by
# shipping a prebuild.
!node_modules/better-sqlite3/prebuilds/**
!node_modules/better-sqlite3/lib/**
!node_modules/better-sqlite3/package.json
!node_modules/better-sqlite3/LICENSE
.git/**
.git/**/*
src/**
webview/**
test/**
scripts/**
out/test/**
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.extension.json
tsconfig.test.json
vite.config.ts
.eslintrc.cjs
*.ts
*.tsx
*.js.map
*.ts.map
*.tsbuildinfo
# Local scratch/staging directories must never reach the package.
.vsix-stage/**
*.vsix
# The packaging OUTPUT directory. It holds finished archives, and anything a user
# happens to put beside them -- sample databases, notes -- which is not extension
# content. Without this, `vsce package` scans its own output directory and sweeps
# stray files into the archive.
VSIX/**
# Local convenience wrappers for running the tooling from the repository root.
# `package.bat` just runs `npm run package`, and `vsce.bat` is a shim that adds
# the output path; neither is part of the extension at runtime.
package.bat
vsce.bat
# Any other dot-directory at the root is local tooling/scratch (backups, caches);
# nothing the extension needs at runtime starts with a dot.
.*/**
# Database files are user data (sample/test databases kept beside the source),
# never extension assets. They must not be shipped inside the VSIX.
#
# The second group matters because SQLite's WAL mode writes sidecars NEXT TO the
# database: `<name>.db-wal` and `<name>.db-shm`. Those do not match `*.db`, so
# without an explicit rule an open database can leak a journal into the package
# even when the database itself is excluded.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.libsql
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*-wal
*-shm
*.journal